.TH DOUBLETAKE 1 "May 2026" "doubletake" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
doubletake \- AirPlay screen mirroring sender for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doubletake
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B doubletake
is an AirPlay screen mirroring sender that streams your Linux desktop to an Apple TV
using the AirPlay mirroring protocol. It supports both Wayland (PipeWire/xdg-desktop-portal)
and X11 screen capture with H.264 or capability-gated HEVC Main10 encoding.
.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 2
Full AirPlay mirroring protocol (RTSP/HTTP + encrypted video stream)
.IP \(bu 2
FairPlay SAP authentication
.IP \(bu 2
SRP-6a pairing with PIN and persistent credential storage
.IP \(bu 2
H.264 encoding with NVENC, VA-API, V4L2 stateful encoders, OpenH264, and x264
.IP \(bu 2
Capability-gated HEVC Main10/high-resolution encoding with NVENC or x265
.IP \(bu 2
ChaCha20-Poly1305 stream encryption
.IP \(bu 2
mDNS device discovery
.IP \(bu 2
Daemon mode with multi-target streaming control via
.B doubletake-ctl
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-target \fIIP\fR
Connect to a specific Apple TV by IP address (skips mDNS discovery)
.TP
.B \-port \fIPORT\fR
AirPlay port (default: 7000)
.TP
.B \-code \fICODE\fR
Pairing PIN shown on the receiver, or its configured password when
"Require Password" is enabled. Prefer the
.B DOUBLETAKE_CODE
environment variable, which keeps the code out of shell history and
.BR ps (1)
output.
.PP
The entered value is retained across reconnects and is used for both SRP
pairing and a later HTTP Digest challenge when the receiver requires both.
.PP
Interactive mode prompts only once after identifying the receiver's security
mode. In the Plasma applet, an on-screen PIN uses a visible four-digit field and
a configured receiver password uses an unrestricted masked field. Doubletake
does not request an on-screen PIN in password mode.
.TP
.B \-port-range \fIMIN-MAX\fR
Confine local timing and audio UDP sockets to a range of at least three ports,
including streams started in daemon mode. Reserve three available ports per
simultaneous receiver.
.TP
.B \-pair
Force new pairing even if credentials exist
.TP
.B \-cred-backend \fIBACKEND\fR
Credential storage backend: \fBfile\fR or \fBkeyring\fR (default: file)
.TP
.B \-creds \fIPATH\fR
Path to credentials file (default: ~/.config/doubletake/credentials.json)
.TP
.B \-fps \fIFPS\fR
Frames per second (default: 30)
.TP
.B \-bitrate \fIKBPS\fR
Target bitrate in kbps (0 = auto, default: 0)
.TP
.B \-target-latency-ms \fIMS\fR
Override both audio and video playout latency in milliseconds. Zero selects the
automatic AirPlay policy with separate screen and audio defaults (default: 0).
.TP
.B \-no-audio
Disable audio for video-only mirroring
.TP
.B \-hwaccel \fIMETHOD\fR
Encoder preference: \fBauto\fR, \fBnvenc\fR (NVIDIA), \fBvaapi\fR
(Intel/AMD), \fBv4l2\fR (stateful V4L2 encoders, common on ARM SoCs),
\fBopenh264\fR (software), or \fBnone\fR (x264, or x265 for
forced HEVC).
Only \fBauto\fR tries fallback encoders. An explicit method fails if its
required GStreamer encoder is unavailable. The default is \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.B \-video-codec \fICODEC\fR
Screen codec: capability-driven \fBauto\fR (default), forced \fBh264\fR, or
forced \fBhevc\fR. Automatic HEVC requires receiver feature 42, a session-time
maximum above 1920x1080, and the complete NVENC Main10/timestamp path;
otherwise it uses H.264 at the nominal canvas. Forced HEVC may also use x265.
The automatic hardware preflight measures sustained 4K capture-to-access-unit
latency and increases both presentation leads by the same bounded margin when
needed, preserving their relative synchronization.
Main10 output does not fabricate HDR metadata for an SDR capture source.
.TP
.B \-debug
Enable verbose protocol logging
.TP
.B \-daemonize
Run in daemon mode for multi-target control via
.B doubletake-ctl
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Discover and connect to any Apple TV on the network:
.B doubletake
.TP
Connect to a specific Apple TV:
.B doubletake \-target 192.168.1.77
.TP
Pair with a PIN (saves credentials for reuse):
.B doubletake \-target 192.168.1.77 \-pair \-code 1234
.TP
Connect to a receiver with "Require Password" enabled:
.B DOUBLETAKE_CODE=... doubletake \-target 192.168.1.77
.TP
Stream with a custom frame rate and bitrate:
.B doubletake \-target 192.168.1.77 \-fps 30 \-bitrate 4500
.TP
Force lower bitrate on weak Wi-Fi:
.B doubletake \-target 192.168.1.77 \-bitrate 3000
.TP
Use hardware acceleration (NVIDIA):
.B doubletake \-target 192.168.1.77 \-hwaccel nvenc
.TP
Use OpenH264 software encoding:
.B doubletake \-target 192.168.1.77 \-hwaccel openh264
.TP
Run in daemon mode:
.B doubletake \-daemonize
.TP
Debug mode with verbose logging:
.B doubletake \-target 192.168.1.77 \-debug
.SH DAEMON MODE
When run with \fB\-daemonize\fR, doubletake runs as a background service that can control
multiple simultaneous connections. Use
.B doubletake-ctl
to manage the daemon.
.PP
Daemon status distinguishes an on-screen PIN from a configured password so UI
clients can present the appropriate single prompt. Both values remain
submittable with the compatible
.B doubletake-ctl pin
command when exactly one receiver is waiting. For concurrent prompts, use
.B doubletake-ctl connect \fITARGET\fR \fIPIN-OR-PASSWORD\fR
to submit a credential to a specific receiver.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 2
Go 1.23 or later
.IP \(bu 2
GStreamer 1.0 (with plugins-base, plugins-good, plugins-bad, plugins-ugly, libav)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBopenh264\fR method requires the GStreamer \fBopenh264enc\fR element
.IP \(bu 2
PipeWire (Wayland) or X11 for screen capture
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/doubletake/credentials.json
Default location for saved AirPlay credentials
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR doubletake-ctl (1),
.BR doubletake-test-receiver (1)
